1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,158
Week four of Sworn, for Tempo Zones.

2
00:00:03,208 --> 00:00:07,742
Last check-in, a test batch's proof was verified on Moderato.

3
00:00:07,792 --> 00:00:10,950
This week: settlement on our own Zone.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:18,674
October sixth: our own Zone's portal settled three proven batches, then our sequencer paid a withdrawal.

5
00:00:18,724 --> 00:00:24,950
October seventh: a forged batch, signed by our sequencer, was rejected on chain.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,950
Then I made the live proofs re-checkable by anyone, with one test command.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,450
What I learned: on a live Zone, proving takes up to half an hour a batch,

8
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:43,200
so the proof sits on the settlement path.

9
00:00:43,250 --> 00:00:46,950
It's necessary, not sufficient: the sequencer still pays.

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,908
Next: this week I ask Zone builders and reviewers if they need this.

11
00:00:52,958 --> 00:00:57,950
I submit October thirteenth, then look for one design partner's batch.
